.TH CCOL_CIRCQ_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_circq_send_zc \- send a message to the queue (it blocks)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_circq_send_zc(ccol_circular_queue *cq, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Waits until the queue has free space and then puts the message in it.
The data is not copied: its ownership moves to the queue, and on
success msg->data is set to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq   Circular queue to send to
msg  Message to send. On success the ownership of the data moves to the
     queue.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - The message was sent
ccol_invalid_args  - cq or msg is NULL, msg->data is NULL while
                     msg->size is not 0, or msg->data is not NULL
                     while msg->size is 0
ccol_not_permitted - Sends on the queue are turned off
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The wait for free space has no time limit, but it ends when sends on
the queue are turned off, because a woken sender checks the send state
again before it goes on. On failure the caller keeps the ownership of
msg->data.

msg->data == NULL with msg->size == 0 is valid and works as a sentinel
message. msg->data == NULL with msg->size > 0 is refused, and so is
msg->data != NULL with msg->size == 0, because a live pointer must
carry a payload.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_circq_try_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_circq_timed_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_circq_recv_zc (3)
